data falsifier_self_host_wet_enrollment_note: String = "Nightly falsifier Wet batch enrollment authority (Wave 2 CI substrate, 2026-07-15; review 44453): falsifier_self_host_wet_entries = template rows (always enrolled when green) PLUS module rows with a restored SelfHostWetReceiptBinding (seed_emitter_behavioral_wet_module_bindings) — disposition-independent so executed wet receipts can re-enroll on the green nightly roster while frontier rows remain SeedRetained until BuildGreen authorization. No binding ⇒ no green wet enrollment. Quarantine expect_red receipts stay on falsifier_self_host_wet_known_red_entries until local wet greens and the binding restores."

data falsifier_self_host_wet_cadence_rehome_note: String = "2026-07-25 REHOME off affected-set falsifier (run attribution on #7199 / srv1-02): template wet receipts are build-verification (emit+cargo), not an affected-set control. Measured: namespace_import_closure ~21min and self_host_logic ~34min against a post-hoc 600s whole-receipt budget (July-15 basis) — wall spent before refuse. Cadence flag false unschedules gunbc_falsifier_plan green Wet batch only; roster retained. Kill-at-deadline LANDED 2026-07-25 (shell waits SIGKILL process group at the ceiling; completion-side backstop retained). Review #7199 OR for batch-2: either reactivate as expect_red with kill-at-deadline, OR park on a separate build-verification cadence with owner+date. Chosen arm: separate build-verification cadence (templates mix already-green ~100s receipts with over-budget ones — a single expect_red batch would unexpected-green the fast rows). See falsifier_self_host_wet_build_verification_cadence_note. SelfEmitted assemble-red receipts are the other arm's live consumer: falsifier_self_host_wet_known_red_entries (Wet expect_red quarantine on the falsifier). LANDED 2026-08-06 (Lane D, still-bat-561): falsifier_self_host_wet_cadence_active flipped true; gunbc_falsifier_plan batch 2 scheduled falsifier_self_host_wet_entries including interpreter_dispatch_bijection_real_roster_witness_test.dag::interpreter_dispatch_bijection_real_roster_red_holds (R1 real-crate bijection). THAT SCHEDULE NO LONGER EXISTS AND THE SENTENCE ABOVE IS KEPT IN THE PAST TENSE FOR THAT REASON (2026-08-26): falsifier.yml and gunbc_falsifier_plan were deleted at 611fd02770/#8283 (2026-08-15), and the cadence flag is deleted with them (falsifier_self_host_wet_cadence_flag_deleted_note). R1 roadmap acceptance was gated on a falsifier-run receipt naming that witness identity — no run can produce one today, so that gate is unmet rather than satisfied, and it was never gated on per-PR bin-witness wet receipts."

// INTERIM home for green-wet TEMPLATE receipts (falsifier_self_host_wet_template_entries) after the
// 2026-07-25 rehome. Owner: #7199 falsifier lane (briansrls). Target date: 2026-08-08 — by then
// either (a) a dedicated build-verification workflow enrolls these rows under
// gunbc_falsifier_self_host_wet_receipt_wall_budget with kill-at-deadline on a sccache-healthy
// runner class, or (b) falsifier_self_host_wet_cadence_active flips true after a dated under-budget
// receipt on that runner class (typed AND). PARTIAL LAND 2026-08-06 (Lane D): arm (b) cadence flag
// only — falsifier.yml gunbc_falsifier_plan batch 2 scheduled the template roster; the under-budget
// receipt leg remained OPEN (operator routing:
// interpreter_dispatch_bijection_real_roster_red_holds whole-transport wall ~692s vs 600s budget;
// witness not shrunk). BOTH ARMS ARE NOW UNMET AND THE TARGET DATE IS PAST (2026-08-26): arm (a)
// never landed, and arm (b) was undone at 611fd02770/#8283 when falsifier.yml was deleted, so this
// INTERIM home has no executor and the roster below is enrolled into nothing. The arm (b) flag is
// deleted rather than flipped, per falsifier_self_host_wet_cadence_flag_deleted_note. Re-adding an
// executor is the reserved operator agreement, not a repair anyone may improvise. Distinct from
// falsifier_self_host_wet_known_red_entries (assemble-red SelfEmitted expect_red quarantine — live
// on the falsifier until the same deletion).

data falsifier_self_host_wet_cadence_flag_deleted_note: String = "THE CADENCE FLAG IS DELETED AT THE ROOT, AND IT IS DELETED RATHER THAN CORRECTED (2026-08-26, dashboard node adhoc-a660c665-d46). WHAT WAS HERE: `data falsifier_self_host_wet_cadence_active: Bool = true` and its reader `falsifier_self_host_wet_cadence_is_active()`, answering whether this cadence has anything executing it. std.witness_admission witness_cadence_has_scheduled_route already answers that same question for all nine cadences from one exhaustive match, and it answers FalsifierSelfHostWet => false, because falsifier.yml -- the sole scheduled executor -- was deleted at 611fd02770/#8283 (2026-08-15). So two carriers answered one fact and they DISAGREED: this flag said the cadence was active while the route gate said it was dark, and the flag had been false-in-fact since the floor cut without anything refusing. That is DESIGN section 3's single-authority violation with a live contradiction sitting in it, and gunbc.ci_layer_roots excl_behavioral_receipt_reason named it explicitly as `disclosed, not fixed, here` -- this row is the fix it deferred.\n\nWHY DELETION RATHER THAN FLIPPING IT TO FALSE, and this is the load-bearing half. The flag fed a fork in v2.workflow.witness_admission consumer_for_explicit_rosters: `if active { FalsifierSelfHostWet } else { OfflineLocalRecipe }`. FalsifierSelfHostWet has no scheduled route, so a row landing there derives DeclaredCadenceUnrealized and reads as UNCOVERED; OfflineLocalRecipe has a route by definition, so a row landing there reads as COVERED. Setting the flag to its honest value would therefore have RECLASSIFIED every roster row from uncovered to covered -- the honesty edit was wired to produce a coverage inflation, which is the DESIGN section 5 absorbing fallback in its purest form: a failure arm that widens rather than refuses. The flag is not a fact that went stale, it is a switch whose false branch fails open, so correcting its value was never available and only cutting the root was.\n\nWHAT THIS CHANGES TODAY: NOTHING, BY MEASUREMENT, AND THAT IS THE POINT. The flag stood at true, so every one of its three live readers was already taking the branch this change makes unconditional -- consumer_for_explicit_rosters returned FalsifierSelfHostWet, witness_exclusion_falsifier_rows_consistent_holds ran its real check rather than its skip arm, and the enrollment predicate below reduced to its fold. The cut removes an authority and a latent fail-open; it moves no row's coverage standing and re-adds no executor. Restoring a scheduled route for this cadence remains a separate, later operator agreement, exactly as std.witness_admission witness_cadence_has_scheduled_route_note reserves it."

fn self_host_wet_entry(entry: String, f: String) -> ScheduleWitnessEntry {
  ScheduleWitnessEntry { entry: entry, function: f, kind: ExecutionWitnessKind }
}

